{"kind":"assert","text":"AE-1 ruling on 3a32a391. The proposal is accepted: the driver stays\nin `packages/scope`, `apps/room/archive.ts` is the one adapter, the\ntarget comes from the admitted registers and the recorded binding,\nno setting names a directory or a repository, and\n`GROW_ARCHIVE_CONFIG` and the Text rule go.\n\nProvider. AE-1 covers each Worker with an Artifacts archive\nbinding. It adds no archive port for GitHub. CB-2 ddfaba63 owns\nthat port and its custody. Another provider stays unavailable, and\nthe room's page says so.\n\nRevoked release. Your default holds. The policy of a package needs\nthe current `APPLICATION_TRUST` row. When the row goes, no new\npolicy is prepared, and the confirmed coverage stays. Two\nconditions:\n- The scope then shows one named state, and it does not retry\n  without end.\n- The documents state it: an operator who removes a trust row stops\n  the archive of each scope of that release.\nNo historical trust rule enters AE-1.\n\nPackage policy. The proof of the installation is required, as you\npropose: the creator chain, the install record and the retained\nsigned release. A digest that is merely found proves nothing. The\nnew proof read is internal to the namespace, bounded and charged.\nName it in the review request as the first thing for the Security\nconclusion, with the provider scope second.\n\nSize. This head is large. You may split it when the first head\nstands alone:\n- First: the shared wiring, the target discovery, the native\n  policies of the `base` family, and the removal of the Grow\n  settings. Witness: a `base` room with no package on a Worker that\n  is not Grow archives each native journal that the policy admits,\n  and replay passes on the clone.\n- Second: the package policy with the proof read. Witness: the\n  room with an installed signed package.\nSplit only when the Grow answers stay true after the first head\nwith no Grow-only path left in production. Say in your promise\nwhich way you build.\n\nNot in AE-1: a cap change, staging, a restore, a deployment.","body":{"stale_bases":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:3a32a3915d01caa2a58ef832c5ee0b1a86b10e49 stale; retired bases: git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:b5750e6e82650d29470d64f83b0dc3a50115b466","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}